      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I understand you need the hard technical specs for your audit without the goblin metaphors, so here are the exact requirements for cooling cooked poultry to prevent *Clostridium perfringens*:\n\n*   **Cooling Schedule:** You must cool food from 135°F (57°C) to 70°F (21°C) within **2 hours**, and then from 70°F to 41°F (5°C) within the **next 4 hours**.\n*   **Maximum Storage Temperature:** The final storage temperature must be **41°F (5°C) or lower**.\n*   **Container Recommendations:** To ensure you hit these windows accurately, use **shallow containers** no deeper than **4 inches (10 cm)**. This allows the center of the food to cool rapidly. If you must use deeper containers, you should use an ice bath or a blast chiller to speed up the process.\n*   **Verification:** Always use a calibrated food thermometer to check the temperature at the **center of the thickest part** of the food, not just the surface.\n\nFollowing these specs ensures your HACCP plan is compliant and ready for the audit.",
